    19	
    20	# Session lifecycle and worktree boundaries
    21	
    22	## Context
    23	
    24	Before the v0.5.0 worktree-first redesign, session writes were ambiguous: session
    25	notes, project memory drafts, and mistake files could land in either the main tree
    26	or a worktree depending on which path the agent constructed. This produced two
    27	documented failure modes:
    28	
    29	- **Concurrent-session corruption.** Without per-session worktrees, two sessions
    30	  working in the same main tree produced overlapping diffs. The manager could not
    31	  tell which file changes belonged to which session, and legitimate work was
    32	  reverted as scope creep at review.
    33	- **Main-tree vs. worktree write-path ambiguity.** The `git/SKILL.md` rule at
    34	  line 33 formerly said "use the main-tree absolute path" unconditionally. A
    35	  worktree-aware agent following that rule would write session artifacts into the
    36	  main tree rather than the worktree, leaving the worktree branch empty and
    37	  producing a PR diff missing the session memory. The inverse failure
    38	  (`codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md`) produced the opposite
    39	  problem — all writes inside the worktree, including transcript paths that live
    40	  in `~/.claude/projects/` and are outside both trees.
    41	- **Session directory placement uncertainty.** Without a canonical rule for where
    42	  the session directory (`sessions/{date}-{session-id}/`) is rooted, agents had to
    43	  guess. Guesses diverged.
    44	
    45	The root cause was that no single rule captured "where does the write go when a
    46	worktree exists?" and "where does it go when one does not?"
    47	
    48	## Approach
    49	
    50	The v0.5.0 worktree-first model resolves the ambiguity with a single canonical
    51	decision made at Configuration Step 1 before any loop work begins.
    52	
    53	**Worktree creation precedes session.json init (D-1).** Row 5 of the
    54	Configuration Step 1 table in `orchestration/SKILL.md` creates the per-session
    55	worktree via `git/SKILL.md § P2` and holds the worktree path in-turn for use by
    56	rows 5.5 (state.json init) and 6 (session.json init). Row 6 stamps
    57	`session.json.git.worktreePath` and `session.json.git.branch`; from row 6 onward
    58	`session.json.git.worktreePath` is the canonical write-root. Branch naming follows
    59	the convention: `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` (e.g.,
    60	`chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9`), where `{ssid-short}` is the first 8
    61	characters of `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. The full branch name is 33 characters;
    62	the slug portion `session-YYYY-MM-DD-{8chars}` is 27 characters, which satisfies
    63	the `git/conventions.md` 3-50 character length constraint on description slugs.
    64	
    65	**`worktreePath` is the absolute write-root (D-2).** The qualified rule in
    66	`git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix and Constraints reads: "Use
    67	`session.json.git.worktreePath` as the absolute root when set; fall back to the
    68	main tree absolute path when `worktreePath` is null (direct mode)." Transcript
    69	paths (`session.json.transcriptPath`) live in `~/.claude/projects/` — outside
    70	both trees — and are never redirected.
    71	
    72	**Per-iteration session-memory commit cadence (D-4).** After each MEMORIZATION
    73	sub-phase completes, the manager commits the iteration's session-memory deltas to
    74	the worktree branch via `git -C "$worktreePath" commit`. Subject:
    75	`chore(session): record {loop} iter{n} memory`. This ensures session memory
    76	survives mid-session abort before Wrap-up runs — `git worktree remove` (Procedure
    77	P5) discards uncommitted state; committed state survives.
    78	
    79	**Direct-mode opt-out retained (D-5).** Row 5 is guarded: when
    80	`settings.git.workflow.mode == "direct"`, the row is skipped entirely — no
    81	worktree is created, `session.json.git.worktreePath` stays `null`, and
    82	`git.branch` is stamped from the current HEAD in row 6. Direct mode is the
    83	documented escape hatch for emergency hotfixes (where the PR lifecycle overhead is
    84	unacceptable) and pure-read sessions (no shippable artifact). Outside these two
    85	situations the default is `worktree-pr`.
    86	
    87	## Consequences
    88	
    89	The worktree-first model is distributed across nine edited surfaces in the skill
    90	tree and session template:
    91	
    92	| Surface | What it carries |
    93	|---|---|
    94	| `orchestration/SKILL.md` Step 1 rows 5/5.5/6 | Row 5: P2 invocation, idempotency 3-state machine, direct-mode guard, branch naming; produces in-turn worktree path. Row 5: footnote — direct-mode opt-out prose (LOCK #5). Row 5.5: state.json init using the in-turn worktree path. Row 6: `git.branch` + `git.worktreePath` stamp source. Smoke-test gate prose. |
    95	| `orchestration/SKILL.md` Step 1 — smoke-test gate | Post-merge verification: `jq -r '.git.branch'` matches `^chore/session-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[a-f0-9]{8}$`; `jq -r '.git.worktreePath'` returns non-null for `worktree-pr` sessions. |
    96	| `git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix | Critical rule (last row): qualified write-path rule — `session.json.git.worktreePath` as absolute root when set; main-tree fallback when null; transcript paths outside both trees. |
    97	| `git/SKILL.md` § P2 — Create worktree | P2 is invoked from Configuration row 5, not from Execution start. Steps for sync, re-verify, create, install, pass path. |
    98	| `git/SKILL.md` § Constraints + Output paths | Constraint: "MUST root session notes and mistakes at `session.json.git.worktreePath` when set." Output paths table: session notes/mistakes row reflects worktree-first vs direct-mode distinction. |
    99	| Five workflow phase docs (`orchestration/workflow/`) | `execution.md`, `ideation.md`, `planning.md`, `preparation.md`, `wrap-up.md` each carry the per-iter session-memory commit cadence (D-4): heredoc commit subject + `AI-Provenance-Record:` trailer + direct-mode opt-out note. |
   100	| `delegation/SKILL.md` | Main-tree boilerplate corrected — delegation prompts reference `session.json.git.worktreePath` rather than a main-tree-absolute path. |
   101	| `orchestration/templates/session.template.json` | `git.worktreePath` and `git.branch` fields present in the template; `git.worktreePath` initializes to `null` (stamped by row 6 at runtime). |
   102	| `preparation/SKILL.md` | Narrow exception extension: executor commits on the worktree branch via `git -C "$worktreePath"` even for promote-now skills (the exception that applies within Preparation). |
   103	
   104	### Validation
   105	
   106	The model is checked at two levels:
   107	
   108	**Smoke-test gate (post-merge check).** After the feature merges to `develop`,
   109	every new `worktree-pr` session must satisfy both of the following checks at
   110	Memorization phase:
   111	
   112	```
   113	# Branch name matches the canonical shape regex
   114	jq -r '.git.branch' .gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/<latest>/session.json
   115	# Expected: ^chore/session-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[a-f0-9]{8}$
   116	
   117	# worktreePath is non-null for worktree-pr sessions
   118	jq -r '.git.worktreePath' .gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/<latest>/session.json
   119	# Expected: a non-null absolute path
   120	```
   121	
   122	A null `worktreePath` on a `worktree-pr` session indicates row 5 was skipped
   123	or P2 failed without surfacing an error.
   124	
   125	**Session writes landing under `worktreePath`.** For any `worktree-pr` session,
   126	verify that `sessions/{date}-{session-id}/` is rooted inside the worktree, not
   127	in the main tree. Cross-check: `git -C "$worktreePath" log --oneline` should show
   128	`chore(session): record * iter* memory` commits appearing on the worktree branch.
   129	
   130	**Direct-mode consistency check.** When `settings.git.workflow.mode == "direct"`,
   131	`session.json.git.worktreePath` must be `null` and `git.branch` must match the
   132	current HEAD at session start. Both `orchestration/SKILL.md` and `git/SKILL.md`
   133	reference `settings.git.workflow.mode` identically (D-5 validation).
   134	
   135	**This session as N=2 witness.** Session `2026-05-24-45388fa9` (the session that
   136	authored this doc) runs in `worktree-pr` mode; its worktree lives at
   137	`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9`. Verifying
   138	that this session's writes land inside that path and that its branch name matches
   139	the regex constitutes the N=2 empirical pass of the smoke-test gate (Bundle B
   140	T1.h, `worktree-create-before-session-stamp.md` § Validation).
   141	
   142	## Rationale
   143	
   144	The single-rule design is grounded in the sessions that have exercised the model:
   145	
   146	- **The `chore` branch-type is the right choice for session branches.** It is
   147	  already in the `git/conventions.md` type registry and correctly signals
   148	  "housekeeping, not a product feature." Future sessions should not re-examine the
   149	  branch-type question; it is closed.
   150	- **Per-iteration commit cadence pays off on abort-recovery.** Because
   151	  `git worktree remove` discards uncommitted state, committing each task's session
   152	  memory immediately after its MEMORIZATION phase means a session aborted mid-loop
   153	  loses at most one iteration's worth of staging, not the whole session.
   154	
   155	## Alternatives considered
   156	
   157	- **`session/{date}-{ssid-short}` branch-type.** Rejected: this type was not in the
   158	  `git/conventions.md` type registry and drew a REVISE verdict from the Codex
   159	  evaluator; the `chore` type was already registered and carried the right "housekeeping"
   160	  signal.
   161	- **Commit session memory once, at Wrap-up.** Rejected: `git worktree remove` discards
   162	  uncommitted state, so a once-at-Wrap-up cadence would lose the entire session's staging
   163	  on a mid-loop abort. The per-iteration cadence bounds that loss to one iteration.
   164	
   165	## Related
   166	
   167	- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/worktree-create-before-session-stamp.md` — the companion design: the worktree must exist before `session.json` stamps git fields.
   168	- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/qualified-git-write-path-rule.md` — the qualified write-path rule (`worktreePath` as the absolute root when set).
   169	- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/per-iteration-session-commit-cadence.md` — the per-iteration session-memory commit cadence (D-4).
   170	- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md` — the direct-mode opt-out that keeps the escape hatch.
   171	
   172	## Source
   173	
